{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{13}{(3x+2)(2x-3)}=\\frac{A}{(3x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(2x-3)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, calculate $A+B.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-10957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13}{(3x+2)(2x-3)}=\\frac{A}{(3x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(2x-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(3x+2)(2x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n13=A(2x-3)+B(3x+2).\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{3}{2}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13 & =A(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3)+B(3(\\frac{3}{2})+2) \\\\ 13 & =B(\\frac{9+4}{2}) \\\\ B & =\\frac{26}{13} \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{2}{3}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13 & =A(2(\\frac{-2}{3})-3)+B(3(-\\frac{2}{3})+2) \\\\ 13 & =A(\\frac{-13}{3}) \\\\ A & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA+B=-3+2=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-10957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "de3faa031d4e8412a943be4223437acc9ddf50fc7444d550c2c285767408c2f7"} {"question" "q-10957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-10957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-10957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-102531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{37-19x}{(3x+1)(x-4)(3-x)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-102531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{37-19x}{(3x+1)(x-4)(3-x)} & =\\frac{A}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{B}{(x-4)}+\\frac{C}{(3-x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(3x+1)(x-4)(3-x)$ gives\n\n$$\n37-19x=A(x-4)(3-x)+B(3x+1)(3-x)+C(3x+1)(x-4).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{3}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}37-19(-\\frac{1}{3}) & =A(-\\frac{1}{3}-4)(3-(-\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\  & +B(3(-\\frac{1}{3})+1)(3-(-\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\  & +C(3(-\\frac{1}{3})+1)(-\\frac{1}{3}-4) \\\\ 37+\\frac{19}{3} & =A(-\\frac{130}{9}) \\\\ \\frac{130}{3} & =A(-\\frac{130}{9}) \\\\ A & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=4$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}37-19(4) & =A(4-4)(3-4) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(4)+1)(3-4) \\\\  & +C(3(4)+1)(x-4) \\\\ 37-76 & =B(-13) \\\\ B & =\\frac{-39}{-13} \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}37-19(3) & =A(3-4)(3-3) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(3)+1)(3-3) \\\\  & +C(3(3)+1)(3-4) \\\\ 37-57 & =C(-10) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-20}{-10} \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{37-19x}{(3x+1)(x-4)(3-x)}=-\\frac{3}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{3}{(x-4)}+\\frac{2}{(3-x)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-102531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "de3faa031d4e8412a943be4223437acc9ddf50fc7444d550c2c285767408c2f7"} {"question" "q-102531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-102531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{2}{(x-4)}+\\frac{5}{(3-x)}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{3}{(x-4)}+\\frac{2}{(3-x)}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{7}{(x-4)}-\\frac{3}{(3-x)}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)}+\\frac{4}{(3-x)}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)}+\\frac{5}{(3-x)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-102531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{3}{(x-4)}+\\frac{2}{(3-x)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-102540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}+7x-24}{(x+2)(x-1)(x+4)}=\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+4)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are real constants, calculate $A+B+C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-102540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+7x-24}{(x+2)(x-1)(x+4)}=\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+2)(x-1)(x+4)$ gives\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+7x-24=A(x-1)(x+4)+B(x+2)(x+4)+C(x+2)(x-1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)^{2}+7(-2)-24 & =A(-2-1)(-2+4) \\\\  & \\,+B(-2+2)(-2+4) \\\\  & \\,+C(-2+2)(-2-1) \\\\ -30 & =A(-6) \\\\ A & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(1)}^{2}+7(1)-24 & =A(1-1)(1+4) \\\\  & \\,+B(1+2)(1+4) \\\\  & \\,+C(1+2)(1-1) \\\\ 2+7-24 & =B(15) \\\\ -15 & =15B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-4,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-4)^{2}+7(-4)-24 & =A(-4-1)(-4+4) \\\\  & \\,+B(-4+2)(-4+4) \\\\  & \\,+C(-4+2)(-4-1) \\\\ 32-28-24 & =C(10) \\\\ -20 & =C(10) \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B+C & =5+(-1)+(-2)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-102540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "de3faa031d4e8412a943be4223437acc9ddf50fc7444d550c2c285767408c2f7"} {"question" "q-102540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-102540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-102540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-346793" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{4x+23}{(5-2x)(x+3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{4x+23}{(5-2x)(x+3)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $5-2x$ |  | $x+3$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-346793" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x+23}{(5-2x)(x+3)}=\\frac{A}{5-2x}+\\frac{B}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(5-2x)(x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n4x+23=A(x+3)+B(5-2x).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-3)+23 & =A(-3+3)+B(5-2(-3)) \\\\ 11 & =11B \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{5}{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(\\frac{5}{2})+23 & =A(\\frac{5}{2}+3)+B(5-2(\\frac{5}{2})) \\\\ 33 & =A(\\frac{11}{2}) \\\\ A & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x+23}{(5-2x)(x+3)}=\\frac{6}{5-2x}+\\frac{1}{x+3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-346793" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "de3faa031d4e8412a943be4223437acc9ddf50fc7444d550c2c285767408c2f7"} {"question" "q-346793" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe57714a"} {"question" "q-346793" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066226/state.json" "file_sha256" "d38285d352fe3ab12d8c77c1cfc258d13bddccd6c6b44b5b79885946fe